                            <comment id="500340" author="simmonsja" created="Tue, 25 Aug 2026 14:07:37 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looking to test this with many flavors of GPU hardware. What would you recommend for NVIDIA and AMD setups?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="500453" author="JIRAUSER19463" created="Wed, 26 Aug 2026 23:24:36 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=simmonsja&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;simmonsja&quot;&gt;simmonsja&lt;/a&gt; any modern NVidia GPU should support p2prdma. However, I don&apos;t know how to set up AI stack based on NVidia GPU to run a real life use case to take advantage of p2prdma (GDS does not use p2prdma).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Internally in our org, we just use a skeleton driver to invoke pci_p2pdma_add_resource() against a GPU device to expose the GPU memory, and use fio to read and write that piece of memory to/from Lustre storage via direct IO.&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
